Then again, what else would they #enhance? Knife? Not really, except as
strictly necessary for survival. They can't two-weapon or ride.
Quarterstaff to expert and unicorn horn ditto is six skills each; dagger
to skilled is three; saber or a gift-unrestricted long sword one. I'd
forget about the unihorn (it's nice, but not nice enough to wield a
two-handed weapon for), and stick to the SoA, thrown daggers, and
Grayswandir or maybe Vorpy or Mjollnir if I get them. 
Counting the needed XL, that's six, three, one and perhaps two for an
emergency knife upgrade. Twelve in total for weapons, if you're being
reasonable and not taking darts to expert or something silly like that.
That leaves you with a skill point left over to take Healing from basic
to skilled, even if you don't level up beyond 14. If you go all the way
to 30 (and why wouldn't you, just for the extra pw), you can take it to
expert, and have 14 points left over for unihorn, short sword, knife to
expert, and both other desirable gift artifacts.

Really, healers are just about the _last_ class to need to worry about
what to #enhance.

